  "rationale": "w107 added GOAL.applyMagic: a mage may spend the month casting one resource-yield node she holds at the world, which costs her that month and her rations and puts materials into the stocks. contentRevision moved 162f80bf169296d0e5fd516cc3c5257a -> d4e3047657b4fa8a1a74e1d52f9f5c86 because autonomy-weight.json gained apply-output-per-month (fp 64) and apply-ration-per-month (fp 4), so this gate refuses on provenance before it reads a metric. METRICS MOVED, AND ON PURPOSE: a month spent applying is a month not spent studying, so the knowledge series fall and the population series do not. At the five-year gate referenceNodesKnown -1.17 (-10.6 SE), referenceKnowledgeInstances -33.14 (-15.4 SE), referenceLibraryDepth -1.465 (-6.7 SE); at the horizon gate referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter moves UP +0.685 (+6.5 SE). Recorded from the branch after merging origin/main, rather than post-merge, because leaving it stale fails verify:full and the ascension Actions job that balance/README.md marks required at release. If a competing baseline re-record lands first this file needs the same treatment again, per the w77 precedent (commit 0cbe5a2, taken from the merged tree). NO NEW RNG STREAM was added (goal selection reuses stream 7 keyed per mage, so contracts.md 6 re-baseline event is avoided), NO WORLD SCHEMA REVISION was needed, and NO GOLDEN FIXTURE WAS REGENERATED. This file is a measurement, not a balance claim: release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0. Both magnitudes ship tuningStatus untuned and are the first two numbers a sweep should move. Record: balance/results-w107-apply-before.txt and balance/results-w107-apply-after.txt.",
